Boot NextZXOS / the TBBlue firmware (the default machine is
\f[CR]next\f[R]):
.IP
.EX
jnext
.EE
.PP
The same, with an explicit SD\-card image:
.IP
.EX
jnext \-\-sdcard \(ti/.jnext/sdcard/cspect\-next\-1gb\-fixed.img
.EE
.PP
Run a program; a bare filename is shorthand for \f[B]\-\-load\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
jnext game.nex
jnext game.tap          # auto\-types LOAD \(dq\(dq
jnext game.sna
.EE
.PP
Run as a plain ZX Spectrum 48K (the 48K BASIC ROM comes from the SD
image):
.IP
.EX
jnext \-\-machine 48k
.EE
.PP
Run at double speed:
.IP
.EX
jnext \-\-speed 200
.EE
.PP
Inject a raw binary at 0x8000 and run it:
.IP
.EX
jnext \-\-inject program.bin \-\-inject\-org 8000
.EE
.PP
Take a headless screenshot, for CI.
Name the SD image explicitly: with no \f[B]\-\-sdcard\f[R] and no cached
image, provisioning prompts on stdin and declines at EOF, so an
unattended run would exit non\-zero instead of capturing anything
(\f[B]\-\-sdcard\-download\-confirm\f[R] is the alternative).
.IP
.EX
jnext \-\-headless \-\-machine 48k \(rs
    \-\-sdcard \(ti/.jnext/sdcard/cspect\-next\-1gb\-fixed.img \(rs
    \-\-delayed\-screenshot /tmp/test.png \(rs
    \-\-delayed\-screenshot\-frames 200 \-\-delayed\-automatic\-exit 5
.EE
.PP
Capture Layer 2 on its own, then the ULA and sprites together:
.IP
.EX
jnext \-\-headless game.nex \-\-delayed\-screenshot l2.png \(rs
    \-\-delayed\-screenshot\-layers layer2
jnext \-\-headless game.nex \-\-delayed\-screenshot us.png \(rs
    \-\-delayed\-screenshot\-layers ula,sprites
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[CR]\(ti/.jnext/jnext.conf\f[R]
GUI configuration, in INI format.
Written by \f[B]Settings > Preferences\f[R].
Host gains are stored under \f[CR][audio]\f[R] as \f[CR]gain_db\f[R]
(master), \f[CR]gain_beeper_db\f[R], \f[CR]gain_ay0_db\f[R],
\f[CR]gain_ay1_db\f[R], \f[CR]gain_ay2_db\f[R], and
\f[CR]gain_dac_db\f[R].
The emulated ESP\-01 is stored under \f[CR][esp]\f[R] as
\f[CR]enabled\f[R] (\f[CR]true\f[R]/\f[CR]false\f[R], the persistent
form of \f[B]\-\-esp\f[R]) and \f[CR]allowed_hosts\f[R] (a
comma\-separated list, the persistent form of \f[B]\-\-esp\-allow\f[R]),
both edited under \f[B]Settings > Preferences > Network\f[R].
Whenever \f[CR]enabled\f[R] is set the status bar carries the ESP cell
\f[B]NETWORKING\f[R] describes, so neither a config file nor that page
can put the guest on the network without saying so.
\f[B]\-\-no\-esp\f[R] overrides it for one run.
CLI options always take precedence over saved values, and headless runs
never read it.
.TP
\f[CR]\(ti/.jnext/sdcard/cspect\-next\-1gb\-fixed.img\f[R]
The default SD\-card image, used when \f[B]\-\-sdcard\f[R] is not given.
.TP
\f[CR]\(ti/.jnext/sdcard/cspect\-next\-1gb.img\f[R]
The canonical distribution image the patched one above is produced from.
.SH EXIT STATUS
\f[B]jnext\f[R] exits 0 on success and non\-zero on error.
In particular it exits non\-zero when a
\f[B]\-\-delayed\-screenshot\f[R] was requested but never taken, rather
than silently writing nothing, and likewise when a \f[B]\-\-record\f[R]
recording fails to materialize as a usable output file.
